# J22 — Evidence loop: setup → authorized Map on the real workload module
#
# Launches against the operator-designated workload module (@TARGET via
# KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET, e.g. ~/monorepo/src/py/cloud — scan target ONLY, never
# patched; the journey removes only kuzushi's own .kuzushi state for
# determinism). Audits the desired setup contract: one readiness check, an
# explicit Start Map commit, live run signal, and an actionable landing.
#
# Fixed by Phase B slice 4 (now expected PASS): the target picker opened from
# the Target row carries the bound target (Enter re-confirms, q/Esc returns
# to Setup with the target intact); the completed run lands on the phase
# RESULT checkpoint; the inventory walk emits heartbeat progress so a
# healthy long stage never shows NO PROGRESS SIGNAL.
name: Evidence loop setup honesty (workload module)
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: rm -rf "@TARGET/.kuzushi"
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 30 READY THE MAP RUN
snap: setup-initial
expect: CONFIRMED
expect: Start Map
expect: Enter Start Map to commit
ask: Setup — one readiness check with the target confirmed and a single explicit commit action; do the signifiers match what Enter actually does from every cursor row?
# The Target row edits, never ejects: the picker opens anchored on the bound
# target, and dismissing it leaves the binding untouched.
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: target-picker-bound
expect: Enter selects: cloud
expect-not: press `d`
keys: q
wait-for: 10 READY THE MAP RUN
snap: setup-after-picker-dismiss
expect: CONFIRMED
# Desired: committing from the footer promise should never eject the target.
# Walk the cursor to the Start Map row (the only row where Enter commits).
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down
wait: 1
snap: setup-cursor-start-map
expect: Commit this Map plan
keys: Enter
wait-for: 30 RUN FOCUS
snap: run-focus-live
expect: MAP
ask: Run focus — live stage labels and progress signal throughout; no NO PROGRESS SIGNAL warning while a stage is actively working?
# Desired landing: the committed Map completes onto the phase RESULT
# checkpoint (receipt + explicit next actions), never back onto the setup
# card that committed it.
wait-for: 240 RESULT
snap: run-complete
expect: receipt ·
expect: Use map
expect-not: READY THE MAP RUN
ask: Landing — after the committed Map completes, does the operator land on the result (receipt + next action) instead of the untouched setup card?
